# The carlos-emr/drugref2026 revision this package builds DrugRef from when
# neither DRUGREF_SRC nor DRUGREF_WAR is supplied. Pin a full commit SHA for a
# release build: a branch name makes two builds weeks apart ship different
# code under one package version.
#
# The current pin carries the free-text allergy fix. Before it,
# get_allergy_warnings dispatched only on the allergy's category type and
# skipped type 0 -- the category CARLOS writes for every allergy added through
# "Custom Allergy", and the one its demonstration dataset seeds PENICILLINS
# allergies with. Prescribing amoxicillin to a patient recorded as allergic to
# PENICILLINS returned an empty warnings array: no alert, no error, and a
# response indistinguishable from "no allergy". A build pinned below this
# revision fails part 3 of scripts/allergy-rx-alert-playwright-checks.js while
# CARLOS itself is correct. The same revision also fixes ATC class allergens,
# which only ever matched a drug's leaf description, so an allergy to a class
# name such as "BETA-LACTAMASE RESISTANT PENICILLINS" never warned on a drug
# filed under it.
#
# NOTE FOR THE MAINTAINER: this is a commit on the fix branch
# (carlos-emr/drugref2026 claude/allergy-search-alert-bugs-q7pcu2), not a
# master merge commit, because the DrugRef change and the CARLOS change ship
# together. Re-point it at the master merge commit once that branch is merged.
#
# It must not be moved back below the previous pin
# (566a46eec559a0ba02f40afbc37ff14440bbc098), the master merge commit of the
# pre-release security hardening (carlos-emr/drugref2026#10), which this commit
# descends from: earlier DrugRef builds ship the bundled `root` superuser
# credential with a password published in that source tree, browser JSPs that
# run a destructive database re-import on an unauthenticated GET and reflect a
# request parameter unencoded, and JPQL built by string concatenation —
# including an unquoted numeric-context injection reachable from the
# unauthenticated XML-RPC surface. It also carries the earlier
# EntityManager-leak fix (carlos-emr/drugref2026#8), without which drug searches
# exhaust the JDBC pool after one or two calls and permanently return
# "None found".
ref=97663b3415cb15a9e7ba0dd3c2be84762e6baa88
